# CLI Command Descriptor

This document describes the `CliCommandDescriptor` model that represents a discovered CLI command.

**Location:** `Models/CliCommandDescriptor.cs`

```csharp
namespace Cyrena.CLI.Models;

public sealed class CliCommandDescriptor
{
    public string Name { get; init; }
    public string? Description { get; init; }
    public MethodInfo Method { get; init; }
    public object? Target { get; init; }
    public IReadOnlyList<CliParameterDescriptor> Parameters { get; init; }
    public bool IsStatic { get; }
    public bool IsAsync { get; }
    public bool ReturnsResult { get; }
}
```

## Purpose

The `CliCommandDescriptor` is created during command discovery and contains all metadata needed to execute a CLI command. It is created by the `CliCommandDescriptor.Create()` method when scanning types marked with `[CliSurface]`.

## Properties

### Name
The command name from `[CliCommand("name")]`.

### Description
Optional description from `[CliCommand(Description = "...")]`.

### Method
The `MethodInfo` for the command method.

### Target
The instance containing the method (null for static methods).

### Parameters
List of `CliParameterDescriptor` for parameters marked with `[CliParam]`.

### IsStatic
True if the command method is static.

### IsAsync
True if the method returns `Task` or `Task<T>`.

```csharp
public bool IsAsync => Method.ReturnType == typeof(Task) || 
                       (Method.ReturnType.IsGenericType && 
                        Method.ReturnType.GetGenericTypeDefinition() == typeof(Task<>));
```

### ReturnsResult
True if the method returns `CliExecutionResult` or `Task<CliExecutionResult>`.

```csharp
public bool ReturnsResult => Method.ReturnType == typeof(CliExecutionResult) ||
                             (IsAsync && Method.ReturnType.GetGenericArguments()
                              .FirstOrDefault() == typeof(CliExecutionResult));
```

## Creation

**Method:** `CliCommandDescriptor.Create(MethodInfo method, object? target = null)`

### Return Type Validation

The `Create` method validates that command methods only use supported return types:

| Return Type | Valid | Description |
|-------------|-------|-------------|
| `void` | ✅ | Simple command, auto-exits |
| `CliExecutionResult` | ✅ | Custom boot flow control |
| `Task` | ✅ | Async command, auto-exits |
| `Task<CliExecutionResult>` | ✅ | Async with boot flow control |
| `Task<T>` (other T) | ❌ | Invalid |
| `int`, `string`, etc. | ❌ | Invalid |

### Validation Logic

```csharp
bool isValidReturnType = 
    returnType == typeof(void) ||
    returnType == typeof(CliExecutionResult) ||
    returnType == typeof(Task) ||
    (returnType.IsGenericType && 
     returnType.GetGenericTypeDefinition() == typeof(Task<>) && 
     returnType.GetGenericArguments()[0] == typeof(CliExecutionResult));

if (!isValidReturnType)
{
    throw new InvalidOperationException(
        $"CLI command '{attr.Name}' has invalid return type '{returnType.Name}'. " +
        $"Allowed return types are: void, CliExecutionResult, Task, or Task<CliExecutionResult>. " +
        $"Method: {method.DeclaringType?.Name}.{method.Name}");
}
```

### Error Example

```csharp
[CliSurface]
public class InvalidCommands
{
    [CliCommand("bad")]
    public int BadCommand() => 42;  // ❌ Throws on discovery
}
```

**Error:**
```
InvalidOperationException: CLI command 'bad' has invalid return type 'Int32'. 
Allowed return types are: void, CliExecutionResult, Task, or Task<CliExecutionResult>. 
Method: InvalidCommands.BadCommand
```

### Valid Examples

```csharp
[CliSurface]
public class ValidCommands
{
    [CliCommand("void-cmd")]
    public void VoidCommand() { }  // ✅

    [CliCommand("result-cmd")]
    public CliExecutionResult ResultCommand() 
    { 
        return CliExecutionResult.Continue(); 
    }  // ✅

    [CliCommand("async-cmd")]
    public async Task AsyncCommand() 
    { 
        await Task.Delay(0); 
    }  // ✅

    [CliCommand("async-result-cmd")]
    public async Task<CliExecutionResult> AsyncResultCommand() 
    { 
        await Task.Delay(0);
        return CliExecutionResult.CommandExecuted(); 
    }  // ✅
}
```

## Parameter Discovery

The `Create` method also discovers parameters marked with `[CliParam]`:

```csharp
var parameters = new List<CliParameterDescriptor>();
foreach (var param in method.GetParameters())
{
    var paramDesc = CliParameterDescriptor.Create(param);
    if (paramDesc != null)
        parameters.Add(paramDesc);
}
```

Only parameters with `[CliParam]` are included. Unmarked parameters are ignored.

## Usage

### In CliService

```csharp
// During registration
var descriptor = CliCommandDescriptor.Create(method, instance);
if (descriptor != null)
{
    _commands[descriptor.Name] = descriptor;
}

// During execution
if (_commands.TryGetValue(commandName, out var command))
{
    var parameters = ParseParameters(command, args);
    var result = command.Method.Invoke(command.Target, parameters);

    // Handle return value based on IsAsync and ReturnsResult flags
    if (command.IsAsync)
    {
        // Await task...
    }

    if (command.ReturnsResult)
    {
        // Return CliExecutionResult directly...
    }
}
```

### Inspecting Commands

```csharp
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromCurrentAssembly();

foreach (var cmd in service.GetRegisteredCommands())
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Command: {cmd.Name}");
    Console.WriteLine($"  Static: {cmd.IsStatic}");
    Console.WriteLine($"  Async: {cmd.IsAsync}");
    Console.WriteLine($"  Returns Result: {cmd.ReturnsResult}");
    Console.WriteLine($"  Parameters: {cmd.Parameters.Count}");
}
```

## Complete Example

```csharp
[CliSurface(Description = "Data management commands")]
public class DataCommands
{
    private readonly IDataService _data;

    public DataCommands(IDataService data)
    {
        _data = data;
    }

    [CliCommand("export", Description = "Exports data to file")]
    public void Export(
        [CliParam("path", Required = true)] string path)
    {
        _data.Export(path);
    }

    [CliCommand("import", Description = "Imports data from file")]
    public async Task<CliExecutionResult> Import(
        [CliParam("path", Required = true)] string path,
        [CliParam("force", DefaultValue = false)] bool force)
    {
        try
        {
            await _data.ImportAsync(path, force);
            return CliExecutionResult.CommandExecuted("Import successful!");
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            return CliExecutionResult.Stop(1, $"Import failed: {ex.Message}");
        }
    }

    [CliCommand("status")]
    public CliExecutionResult Status()
    {
        var status = _data.GetStatus();
        return CliExecutionResult.CommandExecuted($"Status: {status}");
    }
}

// Discovery creates descriptors:
// - "export": IsStatic=false, IsAsync=false, ReturnsResult=false
// - "import": IsStatic=false, IsAsync=true, ReturnsResult=true
// - "status": IsStatic=false, IsAsync=false, ReturnsResult=true
```
